# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

This project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

---

## [v0.4.0] - 2026-06-08

### Added
- Two-factor authentication (TOTP) via Laravel Fortify
- QR code setup with Google Authenticator / Authy
- Recovery codes generation and display
- Password confirmation before enabling 2FA
- `two-factor-challenge` view for TOTP and recovery code login
- `confirm-password` view
- Wizard installer upgraded — now asks:
  1. CSS framework (Tailwind, Bootstrap, None)
  2. OAuth (GitHub and Google)
  3. Two-Factor Authentication
- OAuth buttons hidden automatically when OAuth is disabled (`Route::has` check)
- 2FA section hidden automatically when 2FA is disabled (Fortify feature check)
- `stubs/config/fortify.with-2fa.php` and `fortify.without-2fa.php` for clean config switching

### Changed
- `auth:install` command rewritten as full wizard
- `.env.example` now updated automatically based on wizard choices

---

## [v0.3.0] - 2026-06-08

### Added
- `php artisan auth:install` command — interactive CSS framework selector
- Tailwind CSS stubs (login, register, forgot-password, reset-password, layout)
- Bootstrap stubs (login, register, forgot-password, reset-password, layout)
- None stubs — plain HTML for custom CSS frameworks
- Auto build assets after framework selection
- Warning message to run `npm run build` if styles don't apply

### Notes
- Stubs are kept in `stubs/auth/` and are never deleted — allows switching frameworks anytime

---

## [v0.2.0] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- OAuth login with GitHub via Laravel Socialite
- OAuth login with Google via Laravel Socialite
- `SocialiteController` with provider validation
- Migration for `provider`, `provider_id`, `provider_token` columns on users table
- OAuth buttons on login and register views
- `.env.example` variables for GitHub and Google credentials
- Graceful fallback for users without public name on GitHub (uses nickname)

## OAuth local development note

Google OAuth does not accept `.test` domains. For local testing use:

```env
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:80/auth/google/callback
```

Or use [ngrok](https://ngrok.com) to expose your local app with a public domain.

GitHub OAuth works fine with `.test` domains.

---

## [v0.0.1] - 2026-06-06

### Added
- Laravel 13 base installation
- Laravel Fortify as auth engine
- Livewire 3
- Tailwind CSS 4
- User registration
- Login / Logout
- Forgot password
- Reset password (with log driver for local testing)
- Email verification
- Protected dashboard route
- SQLite as default database
- MIT License
- README with setup instructions
- CONTRIBUTING guide

### Notes
- Fortify is used as auth engine while Breeze/Jetstream don't officially support Laravel 13
- No OAuth, 2FA, or roles in this version — see roadmap in CONTRIBUTING.md

---

